  not the score.'
hypothesis: Completes the state_reset sweep that v042/v047/v048 were SUPPOSED to be.
  Those three came out byte-identical because the recurrent state never carried across
  chunks, so the axis was dead. Now that it is live, the interesting question is whether
  training at the serving horizon (4000) beats training shorter (2000, v051) or longer
  (10000, v052) -- and, more importantly, whether ANY of them beats the unpatched
  v042 at 0.688268, which would price the 4x train/serve memory mismatch directly.
change_vs_parent: training.state_reset 2000 -> 4000 on the PATCHED trainer, plus 1-epoch
  truncation shared with v051/v052 so the three are comparable.
